@@ -33,7 +33,8 @@ and Ankara. Most days there are none; then the map toggle and the list button ar
 - **On the map** — toggle **Show SIGMETs** (next to Show AIRMETs) to draw every active SIGMET
   that has a usable area — valid coordinates with at least part of the area in the region, so a
   neighbouring FIR's SIGMET that reaches well beyond it (Jeddah's, say) is drawn and counted
-  like any other, and the count here always matches the list in **Charts**. Off by default (`defaultShowSigmet`; your choice is
+  like any other, and the count here matches the list in **Charts**: both follow the look-ahead
+  time slider, like the NOTAM and AIRMET layers, and both update when the feed is re-read. Off by default (`defaultShowSigmet`; your choice is
   `navaid.showSigmet`, synced). **Tap an area** to open that SIGMET's card; the area flashes.
 - **The list** — a **⚠ SIGMET** button in **Charts**. It is built exactly like the
   [NOTAM list](#notams): the title with the count, one **Raw / Decoded** switch for the whole
